**What failed:** `tools/ci/offline_verify.sh` failed while compiling `engine_tests`. The errors are in `tests/src/core_assert_tests.cpp`, `core_units_tests.cpp`, and `core_coordinates_tests.cpp`. Those files are US-005 work, and another session modified them at 00:03–00:04 while I was verifying. They use `ENGINE_ASSERT`/`CHECK_THROWS_AS` and `Catch::Approx` in ways that don't compile yet. The CI and offline scripts are not the cause. I did not rerun the offline check because the script deletes `build/linux-dev`, and another session was building in that directory.

**Verified this pass:**
- **Linux/Clang gates:** `ValidateVendor`, `linux-dev`, `linux-debug`, and `linux-unit` (10/10) passed. This ran before the US-005 files appeared.
- **Windows/MSVC gates:** the `win-gate.bat` script passed `ValidateVendor`, `win-dev`, `win-debug`, and `win-unit` (10/10). This run did not include the `core_*` files.
- **CI and offline files:** `ci.yml`, `gpu.yml`, `offline_verify.sh`, and the presets match the acceptance criteria. I made no source changes.

**Still open:**
- **Hosted CI has never run.** The PRD says an OS is not verified until its CI job succeeds, so neither Windows/MSVC nor Linux/Clang counts as verified yet.
- **Compiler pins differ from what was tested.** CI installs clang-14 and gcc-11. The locally verified compilers were clang 10 and GCC 9.4. The PRD requires pinned working versions in CI and docs.
- **Not run:** `linux-gcc`, `linux-asan`/`linux-sanitize`. They would hit the same US-005 compile errors on the current tree. GPU checks are `not-run` because there is no GPU runner. The benchmark check does not apply until US-074.

**To finish:** once the US-005 tests compile and nothing else is building in `build/linux-dev`, rerun `bash tools/ci/offline_verify.sh`, plus `linux-gcc` and `linux-asan`. Then decide whether to pin the CI compilers to the verified versions or document the difference in `docs/build.md`.

